# =============================================================================
# LARGE DATA — never commit
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# flights.csv is ~290 MB. GitHub warns at 50 MB and HARD BLOCKS at 100 MB.
# A blocked push is recoverable; a 290 MB file that made it into history is not
# (it stays in the pack forever and every future clone pays for it).
# =============================================================================
data/raw/
data/raw/*
*.csv

# ...but the three small dimension files and the sample ARE committed.
!data/reference/airlines.csv
!data/reference/airports.csv
!data/reference/cancellation_codes.csv
!data/sample/flights_sample.csv

# =============================================================================
# POWER BI
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A PBIX with 1.9M imported rows is typically 60–120 MB and is a binary blob:
# it cannot be diffed, cannot be merged, and every save adds a full new copy to
# git history. Publish it as a GitHub Release asset instead, and keep the
# reproducible source (M + DAX) under version control.
#
# If you must version the model, use PBIP / TMDL format (File > Save as > .pbip)
# which is plain text and diffable. Then delete the two lines below.
# =============================================================================
*.pbix
*.pbit

# Power BI working files
*.pbix.bak
.pbi/
*.tmp

# =============================================================================
# SECRETS — nothing in this project should need these, which is exactly why a
# stray one must never slip through
# =============================================================================
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
appsettings.*.json
connectionstrings.json

# =============================================================================
# PYTHON
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
out/

# =============================================================================
# OS / EDITOR
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .DS_Store and Thumbs.db in a public repo are a small, avoidable signal of
# carelessness. desktop.ini matters here specifically: this project lives in a
# OneDrive-synced folder and OneDrive writes those files constantly.
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
~$*
*.lnk
.vscode/
.idea/
